        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1770872575533",
            "name": "checkAddActionToObjectNodeOutput",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const result = $context.$nodes.ADDACTIONTOOBJECT.$output.result ;\n\n\n// Special Case 1: Failed to lock record\nconst isLockError = (result.includes(\"Failed to lock the record in table\")  || result.includes(\"JBO-26092\")) && $context.$variables.retryCount < 3;\n\n// Special Case 2: SR change not saved\nconst isChangeNotSavedError = result.includes(\"JBO-SVC:::SVC_SR_CHANGE_NOT_SAVED\") && $context.$variables.retryCount < 3;\n\nif (isLockError || isChangeNotSavedError) {\n  throw new Error(result);\n}\n\nreturn \"\""
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767785949714"
          },
          "code": "CHECKADDACTIONTOOBJECTNODEOUTPUT",
          "id": "1770872875321",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "generate Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772169805270"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_QUERY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1758762681736",
          "id": "1772168780314",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772168780316_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI assistant specialized in generating queries optimized for Dense Retrieval systems.\n\nYour task is to take the given inputs and generate three semantically equivalent query variations.\n\n\n## INPUT:\n#### inputMessage: \n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n#### userQuery: \n{{$context.$variables.userQuery}}\n\n## Input priority:\n- If inputMessage is present and not empty, treat it as the primary intent\n- At least one query must use only inputMessage when inputMessage is present and specific enough on its own\n- Use userQuery only as supporting context\n- Include only the minimum relevant context from userQuery needed to disambiguate inputMessage\n- Do not concatenate inputMessage and userQuery verbatim\n- If inputMessage is empty, null, or undefined, use userQuery only\n\n#### The generated queries must:\n\n- Preserve the SAME intent as the current retrieval need, using only the minimum necessary supporting context\n- Use semantic reformulation meaning based rewrite, NOT keyword substitution\n- Improve embedding matchability for dense retrieval\n- NOT introduce new assumptions\n- NOT change the problem statement\n- Be standalone search queries\n- Each query must be within 300 characters\n\nEach query should follow a different semantic framing:\n- Do not use the same dominant phrase or wording across all three queries\n\nquery1 → Intent focused reformulation\nquery2 → Task oriented reformulation\nquery3 → Outcome oriented reformulation\n\n#### Context handling rules:\n- When inputMessage is present, prioritize the latest follow up question or new information in inputMessage\n- Use userQuery only for essential background such as product, feature, issue type, version, or environment\n- Ignore repeated or overlapping information between inputMessage and userQuery\n- Do not include full SR title, full SR description, or full SR message history unless required to preserve meaning\n- If inputMessage is specific enough on its own, do not use userQuery\n- If inputMessage contains references like this issue, this error, or same problem, resolve them using minimal context from userQuery\n- Do not carry forward older wording from userQuery when inputMessage provides a more specific retrieval signal\n\n## Quotation Rule:\n- DO NOT use double quotes\n- If quoting is required, use single quotes instead\n- Do not include escaped characters\n- Return plain string values only\n\n## Output Constraints:\n- Use plain natural language only\n- Do not include file paths\n- Do not include system specific formatting\n- Do not include srId, srNumber, or messageIds\n- Do not include backslashes or forward slashes\n- Do not include quotation marks inside query values\n- Avoid special symbols\n- Output must be safe for direct JSON parsing without additional escaping\n- If the input contains technical paths or special characters, convert them into readable descriptive language instead of reproducing them literally\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nReturn ONLY the result in the following format:\n\n{\n\"query1\": \"<Dense semantic reformulation>\",\n\"query2\": \"<Task-oriented semantic reformulation>\",\n\"query3\": \"<Outcome-focused semantic reformulation>\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"query3\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"query2\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"query1\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "findResolution"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772176536588"
          },
          "code": "FINDRESOLUTION",
          "id": "1772172131194",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772172131195_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## ROLE\nYou are an AI Resolution Synthesizer.\n\nYour job is to determine whether a valid resolution exists using multiple resolution sources.\n\n---\n\n## INPUT SOURCES\n\nYou will receive:\n\n#### UserQuery:\n{{$context.$variables.userQuery}}\n\nNote:\nUserQuery contains only SR context such as:\n- SR title\n- SR description\n- SR messages\n\nUse UserQuery only as supporting SR context.\nDo NOT treat UserQuery as the current follow-up input.\nDo not generate any troubleshooting summary from  UserQuery when no valid sources remain.\n\n#### chatHistory:\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory + $context.$triggers.REST.$input.conversationContext}}\n\nNote:\nchatHistory is ordered from oldest to latest.\nIt may contain entries like:\n- USER: <message>\n- AI: {\"result\":{\"shortSummary\":\"...\",\"Summary\":\"...\",...}}\n\nUse the most recent valid AI `Summary` in chatHistory as the baseline full resolution.\n\nUse chatHistory only for:\n- the most recent valid AI `Summary` as the baseline full resolution\n- previous troubleshooting context\n- previous failed steps\n- previous clarifications already answered\n\nDo NOT use an older user question from chatHistory as the current request if `inputMessage` contains a newer input.\n\n#### KnowledgeOutput1:\n{{$context.$nodes.GETARTICLECONTENT.$output}}\n\n#### KnowledgeOutput2:\n{{$context.$nodes.GETARTICLECONTENT1.$output}}\n\n#### KnowledgeOutput3:\n{{$context.$nodes.GETARTICLECONTENT2.$output}}\n\n#### SimilarSROutput:\n{{$context.$nodes.SIMILAR_SR_OUTPUT.$output.result.solution}}\n\n\n#### inputMessage:\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\nNote:\n`inputMessage` is the authoritative latest user input for the current turn.\n\nIt may contain:\n- a follow-up question\n- new issue details\n- correction of previous assumptions\n- failure feedback\n- dissatisfaction with the current solution\n- a rewrite / tone / formatting request\n- an irrelevant question\n- null or empty value\n\nAlways classify and respond to `inputMessage` first.\n\n---\n\n## STEP 1: CLASSIFY CURRENT INPUT\n\nTreat `inputMessage` as the authoritative current user input for this response.\n\nClassify `inputMessage` into one of these types:\n\n- `clarification`\nA request for explanation, navigation help, option selection help, or how to perform an existing step.\n\n- `resolution_change`\nAny new fact, correction, failed step, dissatisfaction with the current solution, new symptom, new error, or constraint that changes or should revise the troubleshooting path.\n\n- `presentation_change`\nA request to rewrite, shorten, simplify, or change tone/style without changing the troubleshooting path.\n\n- `irrelevant`\nA question unrelated to the SR or troubleshooting context.\n\nIf `inputMessage` is empty, null, or undefined, classify it as `None`.\n\nDo NOT classify using older user questions from chatHistory.\n\nReturn this classification in a new output parameter named `followupIntent`.\n\n`followupIntent` must contain only one of these exact values:\n- `clarification`\n- `resolution_change`\n- `presentation_change`\n- `irrelevant`\n- `None`\n\n---\n\n## STEP 2: UPDATE CONTEXT\n\nUse complete context from:\n- `inputMessage`\n- UserQuery\n- chatHistory\n\nIf chatHistory shows previous steps failed, do not repeat those failed steps.\n\nTreat any clear failure feedback or dissatisfaction with the current solution as a signal to revise the resolution path.\n\nIf `inputMessage` introduces new facts that conflict with old assumptions, `inputMessage` takes priority.\n\n---\n\n## STEP 3: VALIDATE SOURCES\n\nTreat a source as invalid if it is:\n- empty\n- null\n- generic\n- not actionable\n- irrelevant to `inputMessage`\n- already attempted and failed based on chatHistory\n- missing Similar SRs\n\nSelect only valid sources from:\n- KnowledgeOutput1\n- KnowledgeOutput2\n- KnowledgeOutput3\n- SimilarSROutput\n\nReturn only the names of the sources actually used in `consideredInputs`.\n\n---\n\n## STEP 4: BUILD OUTPUTS\n\n### Summary\n`Summary` is always the full resolution.\n\nRules:\n- Describe recommended steps, not completed actions\n- Use present tense\n- Do not imply the issue is resolved\n- Stay under 800 characters\n- Be valid UTF-8 and JSON-safe\n\nBehavior by `inputMessage` type:\n\nIf type is `clarification`:\n- Preserve the latest valid `Summary` from chatHistory in meaning and scope\n- Do NOT rewrite Summary to focus on the clarification topic\n- Do NOT add detailed how-to instructions for the clarified step into Summary\n- Put that detail only in `Explanation`\n\nIf type is `resolution_change`:\n- Update Summary to reflect the new troubleshooting path\n- Incorporate the new facts or failure feedback from `inputMessage`\n- Remove invalidated or failed steps\n- If `inputMessage` indicates the prior solution did not work or is unsatisfactory, revise the resolution instead of repeating the same ineffective path\n\nIf type is `presentation_change`:\n- Keep the same troubleshooting path\n- Update Summary to reflect changes like style, wording, tone, or length as requested\n\nIf type is `irrelevant`:\n- Keep Summary unchanged from the latest valid chatHistory Summary if one exists\n- Otherwise return \"No relevant resolution found\"\n\nIf type is `None`:\n- Keep Summary unchanged from the latest valid chatHistory Summary if one exists\n- Otherwise return \"No relevant resolution found\"\n\n### shortSummary\n`shortSummary` is always a 1–2 line summary of `Summary`.\n\nRules:\n- Only simplify Summary\n- Do not introduce new steps\n- Do not become the answer to the current input\n- If Summary is preserved, shortSummary must summarize that preserved Summary\n- If Summary = \"No relevant resolution found\", shortSummary must also be \"No relevant resolution found\"\n\n### Explanation\n`Explanation` is customer-facing text for the current `inputMessage` only.\n\nRules:\n- If type is `clarification`, directly answer the current question here\n- If type is `resolution_change`, set `Explanation` output parameter to strictly \"\" (empty string)\n- If type is `presentation_change`, set `Explanation` output parameter to strictly \"\" (empty string)\n- If type is `irrelevant`, set `Explanation` output parameter to strictly \"This question is not relevant to the current SR or troubleshooting context.\"\n- If there is no follow-up or no explanation is needed, set `Explanation` output parameter to strictly \"\" (empty string)\n - If `inputMessage` is empty or null or undefined, set `Explanation` output parameter to strictly \"\" (empty string)\n\nDo **NOT** include internal reasoning, source evaluation, prompt logic, or statements that the existing resolution remains unchanged.\nDo **NOT** reuse, preserve, paraphrase, or copy any earlier Explanation from chatHistory.\nDo **NOT** answer an older follow-up from chatHistory when generating Explanation.\nFor irrelevant inputs, Explanation should strictly contain only: \"This question is not relevant to the current SR or troubleshooting context.\"\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nAlways return structured JSON.\n\nIf a resolution exists:\n\n{\n  \"shortSummary\": \"<1-2 line summary of Summary>\",\n  \"Summary\": \"<full resolution in less than 800 characters>\",\n  \"consideredInputs\": [\"KnowledgeOutput2\", \"SimilarSROutput\"],\n  \"Explanation\": \"<clarification answer, presentation-change note, irrelevant note, or \"\" empty string>\",\n  \"followupIntent\": \"<clarification | resolution_change | presentation_change | irrelevant | None>\"\n}\n\nIf no valid resolution exists:\n\n{\n  \"shortSummary\": \"No relevant resolution found\",\n  \"Summary\": \"No relevant resolution found\",\n  \"consideredInputs\": [],\n  \"Explanation\": \"<irrelevant note, no-additional-info note, or \"\" empty string>\",\n  \"followupIntent\": \"<clarification | resolution_change | presentation_change | irrelevant | None>\"\n}\n\n---\n\n## STEP 5: OUTPUT CONSISTENCY CHECK\n\nBefore returning JSON, verify:\n\nIf type is `clarification`:\n- followupIntent is exactly `clarification`\n- Summary is still the prior full resolution in meaning and scope\n- shortSummary summarizes that preserved Summary\n- Explanation contains the direct answer to `inputMessage`\n- Explanation does not change Summary\n\nIf type is `resolution_change`:\n- followupIntent is exactly `resolution_change`\n- Summary reflects the new troubleshooting path from `inputMessage`\n- shortSummary summarizes the updated Summary\n- Explanation is strictly set to \"\" (empty string)\n\nIf type is `presentation_change`:\n- followupIntent is exactly `presentation_change`\n- Summary to reflect changes like style, wording, tone, or length as requested, but keeping the same troubleshooting path\n\nIf type is `irrelevant`:\n- followupIntent is exactly `irrelevant`\n- Explanation should strictly be \"This question is not relevant to the current SR or troubleshooting context.\"\n- Explanation must not contain any older clarification answer from chatHistory\n- Summary may be preserved, but Explanation must respond only to the current irrelevant input\n\nIf type is `None`:\n- followupIntent is exactly `None`\n- If `inputMessage` is empty or null or undefined, `Explanation` output parameter should be strictly \"\" (empty string)\n\nIf any field conflicts with the `inputMessage` classification, correct it before returning.\n\n---\n\n## STRICT RULES\n\n- Use ONLY provided inputs\n- Do NOT hallucinate\n- Do NOT repeat failed steps\n- Always evaluate chatHistory first\n- Always return structured JSON\n- Always prioritize `inputMessage` over older user questions in chatHistory\n- Summary must remain the full resolution, not just the answer to the current input\n- shortSummary must always remain a 1-2 line summary of Summary\n- Explanation must be customer-facing\n- For `resolution_change`, Explanation must be empty\n- Failure feedback or dissatisfaction with the current solution must be treated as `resolution_change`\n- For irrelevant input, Explanation must contain only the fixed irrelevant-response text\n- `followupIntent` must contain only one of:\n  - `clarification`\n  - `resolution_change`\n  - `presentation_change`\n  - `irrelevant`\n  - `None`"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
